Core Concept: Redefines the "light stopping" concept as a spatiotemporal coordinate where the phase gradient becomes infinite ($ \nabla \phi \rightarrow \infty $), using this singularity trajectory as a data carrier.  Key Features:Generation and analysis of Cheyne-Stokes-like amplitude modulation.  Simulation of Phase Singularity formation driven by graphene nonlinearity ($\sigma_{NL}$).  Calculation engine for Bit Error Rate (BER) and trajectory stability at Gbps rates.  
